    "description": "Mexican Folk Art Collection\nTerracotta Effigy Pipe & Artaluxpan Enamel Plaques\n3 Items, Vintage\nThis vintage Mexican folk art lot includes three decorative pieces inspired by Mesoamerican iconography. The group features a hand-modeled terracotta clay effigy pipe sculpted in Pre-Columbian style, alongside two mid-century Artaluxpan enameled wood plaques illustrating Aztec calendar deities.\nITEMS INCLUDED:\n1.\nTerracotta Effigy Pipe\n- Earthenware clay with painted slip accents, sculpted figure atop a serpent with bowl and stem mouthpiece\n2.\nEnamel Plaque (Xocotl Huetzi)\n- Artaluxpan Mexico, polychrome enamel inlay on wood, labeled on reverse\n3.\nEnamel Plaque (Seated Deity)\n- Polychrome enamel inlay on wood, depicting seated figure with offering vessel\nCondition:\nVery good vintage condition across all pieces. Terracotta pipe shows natural firing variations, light surface wear, and no structural cracks. Enamel plaques retain bright coloration with intact wire outlines; one plaque shows a minor surface scratch on the wooden face. Backing labels and hanger intact.\nOverall Condition\n: All items are USED and are sold AS-IS. Please open a ticket for any questions prior to bidding.\nUsed Item Description\n: Used condition indicates item(s) show signs of regular use, age and may have had repairs or may need repairs. All items featured are DONATED and all sales are FINAL. All BIDS are placed by the buyer with the understanding that this is a donated item that may contain faults unseen by our staff and is ultimately SOLD AS-IS as all information is presented. Items come strictly as pictured and should be assumed to be AS-IS with possible unseen defects. We are\nNOT\nexperts in any field.",
